# Stage 3 Implementation Plan (Revised): Cartesian Equivariant GNN Trajectory Rollout

This document outlines the design and step-by-step implementation plan for **Stage 3: Continuous Trajectory Prediction**. Stage 3 models the time-evolution of dipeptides directly in Cartesian coordinates (positions and velocities) using an Equivariant Graph Neural Network (EGNN), conditioned on the frozen graph embedding $z$ from Stage 1.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Four Pre-Coding Decisions Confirmed in this Revision:**
> 1. **Velocity Source**: The Timewarp `.npz` files do NOT store velocities. We will compute ground-truth velocities using finite differences: $x^v(t) = x^p(t+1) - x^p(t)$ with $\Delta t = 1$ frame (unitless, avoids scale issues).
> 2. **Graph Topology**: We will use a **dynamic radius graph** rebuilt at every rollout step using `torch_cluster.radius_graph` (cutoff ~4.5 Å) with static covalent bonds always included. This is feasible because dipeptides have only ~20 atoms.
> 3. **Single-graph Batch Fix in `adapter.py`**: The `encode_graph` call must pass an explicit `batch = torch.zeros(N, dtype=torch.long)` tensor for single-graph inference so `global_mean_pool` does not crash or return the wrong shape.
> 4. **Additional Evaluation Metric**: We will add **Mean Absolute Deviation (MAD) on backbone dihedral trajectories** alongside KL divergence and Ramachandran overlays. This tests whether the temporal sequence is physically realistic, not just whether the marginal distribution looks correct.

