## Architecture Overview

```
Timewarp .npz trajectory
    x^p(t): [N_atoms, 3] positions (loaded directly)
    x^v(t): [N_atoms, 3] velocities = x^p(t+1) - x^p(t)

Stage-1 Encoder (frozen)
    z: [32]  per-peptide graph embedding (cached to disk)

At each step t:
    Graph G(t):
        - Nodes: N_atoms
        - Node features h_i: atom-type one-hot [8] + FiLM-gated by z
        - Equivariant channels: pos x^p_i [3], vel x^v_i [3]
        - Edges: static covalent bonds ∪ dynamic radius graph (4.5 Å cutoff)

    EGNN:
        FiLM(h_i, z) → rescaled node features
        K × equivariant message-passing rounds:
            m_ij = φ_m(h_i, h_j, ||x^p_i - x^p_j||², e_ij)
            h_i  ← φ_h(h_i, Σ_j m_ij)
            x^p_i ← x^p_i + Σ_j (x^p_i - x^p_j) φ_x(m_ij)
            x^v_i ← x^v_i + Σ_j (x^v_i - x^v_j) φ_v(m_ij)
        Output head → (Δx^p, Δx^v) residuals

    Next state:
        x^p(t+1) = x^p(t) + Δx^p
        x^v(t+1) = x^v(t) + Δx^v
```

