### 2. Data Pipeline

#### [NEW] [dataset.py](file:///c:/VIT_CHENNAI/Computer_science/Internship/MolGraph-AE--main/temporal_dynamics/dataset.py)
`TimewarpCartesianDataset(torch.utils.data.Dataset)`:
- Loads `cache/embeddings.pt` (pre-computed $z$ for each peptide).
- Reads positions $x^p$ of shape `[T, N_atoms, 3]` from `.npz`.
- Computes velocity array: `vel[t] = pos[t+1] - pos[t]` (finite difference, $\Delta t=1$).
- For each peptide, each training sample is a pair `(state_t, state_{t+1})`:
  ```
  {
    "pos_t":   [N_atoms, 3],  # x^p(t)
    "vel_t":   [N_atoms, 3],  # x^v(t)
    "pos_tp1": [N_atoms, 3],  # ground-truth x^p(t+1)
    "vel_tp1": [N_atoms, 3],  # ground-truth x^v(t+1)
    "atom_feat":[N_atoms, 8], # from Stage-1 node features
    "z":       [32],          # frozen graph embedding
    "edge_index_static": [2, E_bonds],  # covalent bond edges (fixed)
    "eq_bond_lengths": [E_bonds],       # equilibrium bond lengths for L_bond
  }
  ```

> [!NOTE]
> **Why store `edge_index_static` separately?** Dynamic radius edges are rebuilt at runtime during rollout because atom positions change every step. Static covalent bonds never change and are always included.

